claims/Claims.tsx:// A person's claims, listed under their row newest first. One form per row adds a claim, or edits
claims/Claims.tsx:// the claim whose editor is open (URL state `editClaim`, the claim's id). Amounts come from the
claims/Claims.tsx:// server as strings with two decimals and are added up in whole cents, never as floats. A claim's
claims/Claims.tsx:// status moves DRAFT -> OPEN -> SETTLED, or DRAFT/OPEN -> VOID; the server refuses any other change.
claims/Claims.tsx:// Opening gives a claim the sheet's next number, which a voided claim keeps; a draft has none.
claims/Claims.tsx:// Only a draft can be edited: to change an open claim, void it and add a new one.
claims/Claims.tsx:// The user who opens a claim is recorded and may not settle it.
claims/Claims.tsx:// Settling fixes a claim's due at the rate of that moment. A person's statement binds each of their
claims/Claims.tsx:// counting claims to the figure it has then, until their next statement; every other claim's due
claims/Claims.tsx:// follows the current rate. Each claim shows the period its date falls in, if any.
claims/Claims.tsx:// A claim with a negative amount is a correction: the form must name, by number, a SETTLED claim of the
claims/Claims.tsx:// same person that it corrects (the server refuses it otherwise). Its due has no floor and no late charge.
